/**
@mainpage AdsBridge Library Documentation

@section intro Introduction

AdsBridge is a shared library that provides a C-API for connecting to one or several Application Data Services within the MATS ecosystem.
AdsBridge is a shared library that provides a C-API for connecting to one or several Application Data Services (AppDataService) within the MATS ecosystem. 
AppDataServices receive signal states from Logic Modules (LMs), which represent hardware components, and then forward them to clients like ArchiveService, Monitor, TestSuite, and AdsBridge. 

AdsBridge facilitates the retrieval of signal states from these LogicModules, enabling interaction with various hardware signals through a unified API.
The library is designed to be used in applications that need to access signal states from one or multiple AppDataServices.

AdsBridge requires configuration within the **RPCT** (Radiy Platform Configuration Tool). User must specify the following configuration options:
- EquipmentID: A unique identifier for the equipment.
- AppDataService(s): The identifier(s) of the AppDataService instance(s) with which AdsBridge should communicate.

@section overview Overview

The AdsBridge library provides a set of functions to interact with AppDataServices

The library provides the following functionality:
- Initialize and shutdown the AdsBridge library
- Configure logging and log levels
- Load and set configurations
- Manage connections to AppDataServices
- Retrieve signal parameters and states

Below is a diagram illustrating the relationship between ADS, LogicModules, and AdsBridge:

\dot
digraph G {
  rankdir=LR;

  subgraph cluster_0 {
    label="FSC";
    color=lightgrey;
    style=filled;
    node [style=filled, color=white, shape=rectangle];
    LM1 [label="LogicModule 1"];
    LM2 [label="LogicModule 2"];
    LM3 [label="LogicModule 3"];
  }
  
  subgraph cluster_1 {
    label="Server 1";
    color=lightblue;
    style=filled;
    node [style=filled, color=white];
    ADS1 [label="ADS1"];
  }
  
  subgraph cluster_2 {
    label="Server 2";
    color=lightblue;
    style=filled;
    node [style=filled, color=white];
    ADS2 [label="ADS2"];
  }
  
  subgraph cluster_4 {
    label="Workstation";
    color=lightgreen;
    style=filled;
    node [style=filled, color=white];
    AdsBridge [label="AdsBridge"];
  }
  
  LM1 -> ADS1;
  LM1 -> ADS2;
  LM2 -> ADS2;
  LM2 -> ADS1;
  LM3 -> ADS2;

  ADS1 -> AdsBridge;
  ADS2 -> AdsBridge;
}
\enddot

@section usage Usage

All AdsBridge API functions are documented in the header file **[AdsBridge.h](@ref AdsBridge.h)**.
<br>
File **[Common.h](@ref Common.h)** contains common definitions and structures used in the AdsBridge library.

<b>Initialization:</b>

The AdsBridge library is initialized using `AdsInit()`. This function also starts a message loop if the application is not Qt-based. Here, the user should provide the EquipmentID of the AdsBridge instance configured in RPCT.
EquipmentID can be later changed by calling AdsSetConfiguration() or AdsLoadConfiguration().

<b>Connection Management:</b>

- Use `AdsAddService()` to establish connections to specific AppDataServices, providing their EquipmentID, IP address, and port.
- Once connections are added, call `AdsConnect()` to initiate communication with all added services.
- Monitor the current connection status between AdsBridge and AppDataServices using `AdsGetTcpConnectionStatuses()`.
- Each AppDataService has two TCP connections: one for signal parameters and states, and one for updating signal states for the most recently observed signals (recents). Therefore, if two AppDataServices are added, AdsGetTcpConnectionCount() returns 4.

<b>Signal Information:</b>

- Use `AdsGetSignalList()` to retrieve the list of signals available from connected AppDataServices.
- Get the total number of available signals using `AdsGetSignalCount()`.
- To calculate the hash value (used for retrieval) for a specific signal ID, use `AdsCalcHash()`. <b>The hash value must be obtained from the AppSignalID.</b>

<b>Signal Data Retrieval:</b>

- After successful connection and signal parameter loading (check with `AdsSignalParamsLoaded()`), use `AdsGetSignalParams()` to obtain detailed information about signal parameters.
- Similarly, after all signal states are received (check with `AdsSignalStatesLoaded()`), use `AdsGetSignalStates()` to retrieve the current state of specific signals.

<b>Configuration:</b>

Full configuration including ADS connection settings can be loaded with `AdsLoadConfiguration()` or set directly with `AdsSetConfiguration()`. Refer to the library documentation for specific configuration options.

The following example demonstrates how to use the AdsBridge library:

@code
#include <AdsBridge/AdsBridge.h>

#include <array>
#include <atomic>
#include <cassert>
#include <chrono>
#include <iostream>
#include <memory>
#include <string>
#include <syncstream>
#include <thread>

struct AppDataService
{
	std::string equipmentId;
	std::string address;
	int port;
};

// EquipmentID of this part of the system.
const std::string g_equipmentId = "TP_MCRWS00_ADSBRIDGE";

// Set to true if this is a Qt application and it runs message loop, otherwise message loop will be run in separate thread by AdsBridge.
const bool g_isQtApplication = false;

// The list of AppDataServices to connect to.
const std::array g_appDataServices = {AppDataService{"TP_WS00_ADS", "127.0.0.1", 13321}, AppDataService{"TP_WS01_ADS", "127.0.0.2", 13322}};

// Exit program flag, is set in the exitProgramThread.
std::atomic<bool> g_exitProgram{false};


extern "C" void log_handler(MatsLogLevel level, const char* message)
{
	const char* logLevelString = nullptr;
	switch (level)
	{
	case LOG_LEVEL_DEBUG:
		logLevelString = "DBG: ";
		break;
	case LOG_LEVEL_WARNING:
		logLevelString = "WRN: ";
		break;
	case LOG_LEVEL_ERROR:
		logLevelString = "ERR: ";
		break;
	default:
		logLevelString = "UNK: ";
		break;
	}

	std::osyncstream{std::cerr} << logLevelString << message << "\n";
	return;
}

void dumpAppSignalState(const MatsAppSignalState& state, std::string_view appSignalId)
{
	std::cout << "AppSignalState: " << state.value << (state.flags & MATS_FLAG_VALID ? " (VALID)" : " (NOT_VALID)");
	if (appSignalId.empty() == false)
	{
		std::cout << " - " << appSignalId;
	}
	std::cout << "\n";

	std::cout << "\thash: " << std::hex << state.hash << std::dec << "\n";

	std::cout << "\tflags: ";
	std::cout << (state.flags & MATS_FLAG_VALID ? "VALID" : "NOT_VALID ");
	std::cout << (state.flags & MATS_FLAG_STATE_AVAILABLE ? "" : "STATE_NOT_AVAILABLE ");
	std::cout << (state.flags & MATS_FLAG_SIMULATED ? "SIMULATED " : "");
	std::cout << (state.flags & MATS_FLAG_BLOCKED ? "BLOCKED " : "");
	std::cout << (state.flags & MATS_FLAG_MISMATCH ? "MISMATCH " : "");
	std::cout << (state.flags & MATS_FLAG_ABOVE_HIGH_LIMIT ? "ABOVE_HIGH_LIMIT " : "");
	std::cout << (state.flags & MATS_FLAG_BELOW_LOW_LIMIT ? "BELOW_LOW_LIMIT " : "");
	std::cout << (state.flags & MATS_FLAG_SW_SIMULATED ? "SW_SIMULATED " : "");
	std::cout << (state.flags & MATS_FLAG_TUNING_DEFAULT ? "TUNING_DEFAULT " : "");
	std::cout << "\n";

	std::cout << "\tplantTime: " << state.plantTime << "\n";
	std::cout << "\tserverTime: " << state.serverTime << "\n";

	return;
}

int main(int argc, char* argv[])
{
	AdsSetLogHandler(log_handler);
	AdsSetLogLevel(LOG_LEVEL_DEBUG);

	// Initialize, create QCoreApplication, start Qt message loop if g_isQtApplication is false!
	bool initOk = AdsInit(argc, argv, g_equipmentId.c_str(), g_isQtApplication);
	if (initOk == false)
	{
		std::cerr << "Failed to initialize AdsBridge.\n";
		return EXIT_FAILURE;
	}

	// Adding service does not start communication, it just adds service to the list.
	for (const auto& ads : g_appDataServices)
	{
		AdsAddService(ads.equipmentId.c_str(), ads.address.c_str(), ads.port);
	}

	// Connects to all added services.
	AdsConnect();

	// This thread waits for user input to exit the program.
	std::jthread exitProgramThread{[]()
								   {
									   std::string input;
									   std::getline(std::cin, input);
									   g_exitProgram.store(true);
								   }};

	// Wait until all signal params and states are loaded or timeout occurs.
	{
		using namespace std::chrono;
		const auto timeout = seconds(15); // Loading signal params and states can take some time.
		auto start = steady_clock::now();

		while (steady_clock::now() - start < timeout && g_exitProgram.load() == false)
		{
			if (AdsSignalParamsLoaded() == true && AdsSignalStatesLoaded() == true)
			{
				break; // All signal params and states are loaded.
			}

			std::this_thread::sleep_for(milliseconds(250));
		}

		if (AdsSignalParamsLoaded() == false || AdsSignalStatesLoaded() == false)
		{
			std::cerr << "Failed to load all signal params and/or states.\n";
			return EXIT_FAILURE;
		}
	}

	// Get signal list.
	size_t signalCount = AdsGetSignalCount();
	std::cout << "Signal count: " << signalCount << "\n";

	auto signalHashes = std::make_unique<MatsSignalHash[]>(signalCount);
	auto signalParams = std::make_unique<MatsAppSignalParam[]>(signalCount);

	// AdsGetSignalList returns all signal hashes to `signalHashes` which AppDataServices have access to.
	// Signal hashes are used to get signal params and states.
	bool getOk = AdsGetSignalList(signalHashes.get(), signalCount);
	if (getOk == false)
	{
		// Can fail if another ADS is just connected since last call of AdsGetSignalCount(),
		// mitigation: try again, but demo just exits.
		std::cerr << "Failed to get signal list.\n";
		return EXIT_FAILURE;
	}

	// Get signal params, input signalHashes, output signalParams, input signalCount allocated by caller (signalParams).
	getOk = AdsGetSignalParams(signalHashes.get(), signalParams.get(), signalCount);
	if (getOk == false)
	{
		std::cerr << "Failed to get signal params.\n";
		return EXIT_FAILURE;
	}

	// -- Loop, print some info, exit if user hits Enter. --

	// Signal IDs to get states for.
	std::array signalIds{"#AZPZ_RACK1_CH01_MD00_CTRLIN_INH02A", "#AZPZ_RACK1_CH01_MD00_CTRLIN_INH03A"};

	// Calculate hashes for signal IDs.
	std::array hashes{AdsCalcHash(signalIds[0]), AdsCalcHash(signalIds[1])};

	// Allocate buffer for signal states.
	std::array<MatsAppSignalState, hashes.size()> states{};

	while (g_exitProgram.load() == false)
	{
		AdsGetSignalStates(hashes.data(), states.data(), states.size());

		dumpAppSignalState(states[0], signalIds[0]);
		dumpAppSignalState(states[1], signalIds[1]);

		std::cout << "\nHit Enter to exit...\n";
		std::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::milliseconds(1000));
	}

	// Close all connections, shutdown, stop Qt message loop.
	//
	AdsCloseConnection();
	AdsShutdown();

	return EXIT_SUCCESS;
}
@endcode

@section api API Reference

For detailed API documentation, please refer to the following header files:
- @ref AdsBridge.h
- @ref Common.h

